maria: Heads up — PR #4213 is ready but I want to add a tiny example for parse fallback behavior when the model returns malformed JSON. Quick review? :eyes:

aj: Sending a quick pass. Can you paste the minimal example you want? I think a short JS + Python snippet should be enough.

maria: Yep. Idea is to show 1) schema validation failing, 2) attempt to parse, 3) fallback to a 'text' field and surface an error metric. Something like:

maria: ```js
// pseudo-js snippet for docs
const resp = await client.call({ input: prompt, schema: mySchema });
try {
  const parsed = JSON.parse(resp.output);
  // validate(parsed) -> pass
} catch (e) {
  // fallback: use resp.text fallback and flag as parse_failure
}
```

lucy: love that. For the SDK snippets we should use the official client helpers though — show the new parseWithSchema helper, then show a manual fallback. Otherwise ppl copy the old pattern.

devon: I'll update the example to use parseWithSchema. Also note a link in the PR points to the old 'schema guide' URL. I can fix that and add a redirect note.

maria: thanks. Can you also add a short note about beaconing a metric (parse_failure) so users can alert on regressions? Maybe a one-liner plus pointer to the monitoring page.

aj: For the monitoring pointer, use /console/metrics/docs/parse-failures. I'll add a small graph screenshot placeholder.

sam: We should add an integration test in docs-e2e that runs the snippet against a mocked model that returns invalid JSON and asserts the fallback path. I can wire that up.

maria: Perfect. Dev, Lucy, Aj, Sam — who's taking the PR? I can shepherd but won't be able to push commits today.

devon: I can push small fixes (links + switch to parseWithSchema).

lucy: I'll craft the JS + Python snippets and ensure they match the SDK surface (and add a tiny note about function calling vs structured output differences).

aj: I'll add the monitoring link and the screenshot placeholder.

sam: I'll add the e2e test and a short CI job to run it on docs-changes.

maria: awesome. One more ask — can we include a short 'migration note' for anyone moving from the old parse->validate flow to parseWithSchema, like: "If you relied on try/parse for validation, switch to parseWithSchema to get deterministic schema errors + telemetry."

devon: will add that under 'Migration notes' with a small code diff.

maria: timeline: aiming to merge by EOD tomorrow. If anyone hits blockers ping me and I'll reassign. :sparkles:

docs-bot: Reminder — PR #4213 has been assigned reviewers: @lucy, @devon, @aj, @sam. CI job docs-e2e-integration queued.

aj: Quick question — do we want to include an explicit `content-type: application/json` example for webhook consumers? Some of our users are confused when they receive text fallback.

lucy: yes, add a small paragraph: "If you POST results to webhooks, include a content-type and check for parse_failure flag; treat text fallback as human-readable fallback, not machine-parseable JSON."

maria: great. ok — I'll open a tiny follow-up PR if devon/lucy/sam want to land larger changes. Thanks all! :raised_hands:
